WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.650
Our Try Fighters team has made it through

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.190
round one of the Gunpla Battle Championship West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.320
Let's toast to our victory.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.490
With kiddy juice, of course.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.070
Cheers!

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.990
Miss Hoshino. how was the match?

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.830
It was an easy victory!

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.870
I wouldn't go that far, but...

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.130
I think we all showed our individual traits in a good way.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.420
You're right.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.420
The battle was really worth seeing.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.810
Yuuma's Lightning Gundam has added transformation features.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.480
Sekai has become one with the Build Burning Gundam,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.150
enough to use the Jigen Haoh style of kenpo in space.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.320
And there was Fumina's Winning Gundam.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.910
When it transformed from a core booster to a mobile suit,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.000
the audience at the venue must've been suprised.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:13.420
Fumina, it looks like there are more hidden functions in this machine.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.090
That's still a secret.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.220
You sound like a big-time player.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.680
Why are you in the championships?

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.940
Are you trying to flee from competing with me?

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.020
Hey, answer me, Yuuma!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.860
Kousaka, what's wrong? You look spaced-out.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.650
Oh, no.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.820
It's nothing.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.390
<i>Teams in the Under-19 division consist of 3 people.</i>

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.810
<i>You can deploy up to 3 mobile suits.</i>

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.730
<i>Non-mobile suit support machines also count as one unit.</i>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:39.070
<i>A mobile suit that docks and transforms is counted as one, but...</i>

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.910
<i>when separated, all these parts must be controlled by one person.</i>

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.200
<i>A team may only deploy one powerful large mobile armor.</i>

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.370
<i>All three members must control it together.</i>

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.340
<i>The machines used in battle can be changed for each match.</i>

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.470
<i>But changing machines during battle is forbidden.</i>

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.340
<i>Battlefields are chosen randomly by the system's AI.</i>

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.100
<i>The regulation time for one match is 15 minutes.</i>

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.230
<i>To win, a team must destroy all the other team's machines.</i>

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.480
<i>or have more machines left when the times runs out.</i>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.110
<i>If both teams have the same number of machines left, meaning the battle is a tie,</i>

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:27.410
<i>representatives of each team will fight one-on-one to decide the winner.</i>

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:34.080
<i>Everybody, let's remember the rules of the tournament, and have a fun Gunpla battle!</i>

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.670
Why are we watching this now?

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.050
Sekai didn't understand when I explained verbally.
So I thought I'd show hime this video.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.550
Sekai, do you get the rules now?

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.930
He's sleeping!

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.310
Hoshino, you should give up.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.980
Just like how anything multiplied by zero is still zero,

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.650
anything that a fool does will still be foolish.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.900
I'm home!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.990
Miss Mirai's back.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.660
Sorry I didn't serve you any drinks. I'll prepare some right now.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.160
Please don't mind us.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.120
I'll help you.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.870
You don't need to do that.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.620
Mr. Ral.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.710
Why...?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.000
I ran into him in the shopping district.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.170
Everyone. Your opponent for round two has been decided.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.760
Our opponent?

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.390
Who is it, Mr Ral?

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.520
The Science Club from Seire n Technical College.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.100
Seiren Technical College.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.560
Seiren Technical? You mean...!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:41.480
Yes. Though they don't have a Plastic Model Club, they've won many robotics contests.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:46.950
Even in Gunpla Battle, that team is considered a favorite to win the championship.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.780
So they're strong. I love to fight opponents like that!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.410
I have the tournament video from last year.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.330
Seiren Technical College's battle should be on it.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.750
Then let's watch it and prepare.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.670
It's pointless.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:06.630
Seiren change their Gunpla in every tournament, no, every match.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.140
Having prior knowledge about them might be an obstacle later.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:10.720
But--

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.430
As long as we're strong, that'll be fine, right?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.350
Well... you're right, but...

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.440
Keep your guards up.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:24.610
Many teams who have fought against Seiren say of them,

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:32.530
"Whatever tactics we tried, they read our next moves, and drove us to defeat."

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.040
<i>"Seiren rules the battlefield."</i>

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.880
Team Try Fighters.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.750
Of course, the one we should focus on is Yuuma Kousaka.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.800
I would think so.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.420
Not just for his machine's quality,

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:53.800
but he also fought in the national tournament when he was in elementary school.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.060
So he has great skills as a fighter, too.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.020
He's a tough customer for sure.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:06.940
But putting it another way, if we keep Yuuma kousaka in check, then our victory is assured.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.610
Coach.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:13.740
The other two are a martial artist with no ranged weapons, and an SD Gundam.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.950
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.460
Nishikawa, you're a natural genius at electronic engineering.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.000
Show them the power of your new weapons.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.000
Yes, sir.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:29.010
Okamoto, you're top of your class in formation science.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.970
Gather intelligence on that team and predict their battle strategy.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.050
Okay, sir.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.730
And Ishibashi, as the overseas-trained ace of the Nautical Department,

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.520
you'll destroy the opponents and smash them to pieces!

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.230
Yes, sir!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.900
Our Seiren Technical College Science Club will win.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.530
Thank you very much.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:08:00.620
Seiren is a strong opponent. They made it to the national tournament three years ago.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.330
If we can win, we'll be closer to the nationals as well.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.710
Welcome...

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.090
Sakai Minato!?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.510
What's with that face? I'm a customer, you know.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.640
Can't you smile nicely?

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.230
If you don't like it, you can leave.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.560
We can also choose our customers.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.940
What a big mouth.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.110
Then I'll have an reiko.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.030
Reiko? What's that?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.360
Reiko means iced coffee.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.660
Don't you know even know that?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.330
Tokyo people have no common sense.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.540
So why are you here?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.590
You didn't tell me why you started playing Gunpla Battle.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.260
Tell me why.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.470
To keep a promise that I made to somebody.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.640
And to get back something I had lost.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.600
What an elaborate reason.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.900
I'll use that line somewhere else.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.400
Do whatever you like.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.230
But your battle ends in two days.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:16.070
There's no way your team can defeat Seiren Technical College in round two.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.160
And why are you so sure?

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:20.740
It's obvious.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:26.540
Even if each machine is good, you all fight as individuals.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:32.300
If you don't coordinate as a team, you can't win at Gunpla Battle.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.390
Hurry up and admit your battling is useless!

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.100
You should concentrate on the Master Cup in August!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.770
The builder's contest?

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:47.100
That's right! That's where we'll fight to see who's better!

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.400
If you don't enter the contest, there's no point in me winning.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.620
Yes. this is Kousaka.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.790
Hoshino?

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.870
What's the matter, Hoshino?

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.250
Why did you call us this late?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.090
And you asked us to bring Gunpla.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.920
I want you both to see this.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.220
The hidden power of Winning.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.140
The power of Winning?

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:21.930
That's right.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:26.310
We'll definitely need this power in the second round.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.440
<i>Field 13, Tundra.</i>

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.280
<i>Mock battle model, deployed.</i>

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.620
I-It's huge!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.660
A Mega Size?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.540
I'll go for it!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.080
Watch carefully!

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.260
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.220
Hoshino.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:07.850
That was...

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.060
This is the path that to victory that I came up with.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.900
The Winning Road.

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:21.110
We now begin match three of the second round of the West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:37.420
With such a weak attack, it's impossible for you...

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:42.930
to leave a scratch on this R-Gyagya's shield!

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.470
That's right.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.270
I totally agree!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.270
N-No way.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.950
Shield! Shield! Shield!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.080
My shields!!

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.330
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:19.710
The winner of match three is St. Odessa Girls' School, team Song Dynasty Vase.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.880
We got through round two.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.340
I'm totally stoked.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.890
I'll give this victory to...

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.060
You, Sekai!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:30.720
Well, I don't really want it.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.230
Wh-

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.980
What!? But that's so...!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.310
That's so mean!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:39.070
<b>But you're still cool!</b>

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.860
That's so dejecting!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.280
Hoshino, where's Mr. Ral?

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:47.200
He sent me an e-mail, saying he overslept so he'll be late.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.910
Just when we need his advice.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.830
We'll just have to win!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.170
You're right.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:02.300
If we can't get through this situation on our own, the nationals would be only be a dream.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>We will now continue to the fourth match.</i>

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:09.470
<i>Team Try Fighters from Seiho Academy Middle School</i>

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:14.390
<i>versus team SRSC from the Seiren Metropolitan Techincal College.</i>

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.230
Yuuma.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.980
Just you wait and see...

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.150
the power of Seiren.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:27.360
Now, let's rule the battlefield!

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.490
Yes, sir.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.540
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, startup.</i>

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.710
<i>Model damage level, set to B.</i>

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.250
<i>Please set your GP base.</i>

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.340
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.350
<i>Field 3, Forest.</i>

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.600
<i>Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.690
Those machines! They're based on the Ez8 from "The 08th MS Team".

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.690
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.950
Hoshino Fumina, Winning Gundam.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.990
Kousaka Yuuma, Lightning Gundam.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:15.410
Kamiki Sekai, Build Burning Gundam.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.160
Team Try Fighters!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.960
Let's go!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.090
Don't be too careless and go too far ahead.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.760
We'll wait for them to make the first move.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:29.760
Roger that.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:30.470
Yeah.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.850
This is Unit 3. Enemy has been acquired.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.520
They are at Point TE32.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.440
Looks like we can go with Plan 26.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.980
All units, go to wired communication.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.190
Unit 2, stand by at planned point.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.280
Unit 3, spread out the bugs!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:50.160
Roger that!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.120
What's that light?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.620
A particle disruption screen?

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.130
Are they trying to block our long-range beams?

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.550
Then let's get in close!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.710
That's what they'd think.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:12.680
You're already under our rule. Try Fighters!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.810
There's no attack from the enemy.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.520
I don't like this kind of fight.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.070
If you're a man, fight fair and square!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.650
This is also a form of tactics.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.400
Not everybody's a brainless microbe like you.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:30.860
What did you say!?

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.200
The communications cut off!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.490
What's going on?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.250
A jamming system!?

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.170
From the rear!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.590
You're in the way, Sekai!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:51.800
Darn, he can't hear me.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.260
Where are they firing from?

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.810
No enemy machines.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.020
Could it be...?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:08.530
Optical camouflage!?

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.870
We're pinned down in the jamming area.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.370
Where're you going, Sekai!?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.620
Don't hide. Come out and fight!

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.500
Kamiki Sekai has excellent physical abilities.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.460
But his personality is impulsive.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.380
So his actions are reckless!

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.220
How dare you...!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.520
They're seperated. Go, unit 2!

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.730
Roger that.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.190
That's nothing!

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.120
How's that?

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:04.830
That explosion...!

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.000
Did they get him?

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.630
Sekai!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.550
Hoshino Fumina.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.220
She's the Battle Club president and team leader.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.590
And...

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.760
She cares for her friends.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.640
Exactly what our data says!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:28.940
Hoshino!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.750
Yuuma is careful, so he won't come out recklessly.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:49.960
They developed their tactics based on the fighters' personalities, not just the machines' traits.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.630
Seiren is ruling the battlefield.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.690
Plavsky craft!?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.850
No wonder they're favourites.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.520
But we still have the Winning Road.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.320
I believe in you guys, Sekai, Yuu!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.360
I have you now!

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.120
I did it!

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.000
A direct hit.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.750
It separated at the last minute!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.370
What!?

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.800
Just like yesterday...

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.710
Oh no!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.010
That's Hoshino's part!

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.770
Winning Knuckle!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:49.980
What!?

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:51.270
They docked!?

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.570
Jigen Haoh style!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.860
Dangan Hagan-Ken!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.860
<i>Dangan Hagan-Ken: Bullet Rock-Breaking Fist</i>

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.580
No way!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.370
What an impact!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.000
The optical camouflage!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.380
That's so reckless.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:15.170
Yuu.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:16.000
The comms are back!

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.210
Use this!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.130
What's that?

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.880
I won't let you!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.770
He's locked on to me!?

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.690
Sorry. I'm already out of range.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.940
You believe you've got away,

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.450
but this Winning Launcher...

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.280
can reach you!

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:50.460
U-Unbelievable!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:53.920
Unit 2 has been!

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.090
It's payback time!

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.850
I don't have any data on this!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.350
Even Unit 3 has been.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.110
Now you're finished!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:24.740
Jigen Haoh style! Shippuu-Zuki!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:24.740
<i>Shippu-Zuki: Gale Punch</i>

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.540
Impossible. We must rule the battlefield...!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.300
<i> Battle ended.</i>

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:48.850
<i>The winner of match four is Seiho Academy Middle School, team Try Fighters.</i>

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.520
He did it!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.560
We did it.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.150
Well done, Fumi.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.360
We're sorry, Coach.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.950
No way.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:09.080
Our team is the ruler of the battlefied. How could we lose a match...

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.450
<i>You're late, Mr. Ral!</i>

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.160
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.040
I forgot to set the alarm.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:18.540
L-Lieutenant Ral!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:23.260
Still, well done. Congratulations on clearing the second round.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.760
<b><i>The Blue Giant is their...!?</i></b>

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.090
T-Total defeat.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.060
That was great teamwork.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.310
That's not it.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.400
It's that SD.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.070
It made the other two work together.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.530
That Gunpla was built cleverly as a tool to do that.

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.570
That girl...

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.160
She is good.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:36.060
Yo, who's the president of this club?

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:37.310
What do you want?

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:38.850
Where is he?

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:42.020
Sudou, a guest for you.

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:43.690
What is it?

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:45.770
I'm Suga Akira.

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:48.530
I've just been transferred here.

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:50.650
Transferred?

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:53.740
I'm a transfer student. Nice to meet you.

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:59.120
So, where do I bunk down?

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.330
Everyone has a reason to fight.

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:03.290
We have a reason.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:04.630
Our opponent, too.

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:06.630
Next Episode, "Straight-Build Shimon."

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.210
But this battle is too bitter.
